\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
If a Riemannian manifold has no conjugate points, must its underlying smooth manifold admit some Riemannian metric with nonpositive sectional curvature? The new metric need not be the original one.

\subsection{Short English statement}
If a Riemannian manifold has no conjugate points, must its underlying smooth manifold admit some Riemannian metric with nonpositive sectional curvature? The new metric need not be the original one.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 20001881 (AIM-GEOMETRY-0219). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.
\url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
\item[S2] Original problem formulation and mathematical context.
\url{https://aimath.org/pastworkshops/geodesicsproblems.pdf}.
\end{itemize}
\label{end:20001881}

